  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by virtue of its forward projection and awkward roof configuration would appear visually incongruous and out of keeping with the host building, resulting in less than substantial harm to the character and appearance of both the property and this part of The Meadway Conservation Area. Insufficient information has been submitted with regards to the junction between the existing chimney and the proposed development.  The proposal would fail to preserve or enhance the character and appearance of the Conservation Area contrary to Section and 72(1) of the Planning (Listed Buildings and Conservation Areas) Act 1990. The harm caused is not outweighed by public benefits and therefore fails to accord with Section 16 of the National Planning Policy Framework 2024; Policy HC1 of the London Plan 2021; Policies 37 and 44 of the DMD 2014; Policy 31 of the Core Strategy 2010 and the Meadway Conservation Area Character Appraisal."
